usb-guide-vendor = The device now uses the vendor driver { $driver }. Replacing it with WinUSB disables the vendor's program for this device.
usb-guide-winusb-1 = Download the free Zadig tool (zadig.akeo.ie). BurnCraft does not include it.
usb-guide-winusb-2 = Run Zadig, tick “List All Devices” in the Options menu and select the device with USB ID { $ids }.
usb-guide-winusb-3 = Choose WinUSB as the target driver and click “Install Driver” (or “Replace Driver”).
usb-guide-winusb-4 = Unplug and replug the laser, then click “Find my laser”.
usb-guide-ch341 = Instead of WinUSB you can keep the original CH341 vendor driver (CH341DLL): BurnCraft can also reach the K40 through it.
usb-guide-udev-1 = Save the udev rules: burncraft-cli udev | sudo tee { $path }
usb-guide-udev-2 = Reload the rules: sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
usb-guide-udev-3 = Unplug and replug the laser, then click “Find my laser”.
usb-guide-busy = Close other programs that use the laser (e.g. the vendor's program) and click “Find my laser”.
